# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Personal Claude Code config (the hook script itself IS tracked, so the
# automation is visible to anyone reading the repo; only local settings are not).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Nothing under "main scroll folder" is ignored on purpose.
#
# The frame sequences ARE the site: js/journey.js draws them to a canvas, and
# without them the pinned journey renders as a black box. They are generated by
# scripts/media-pipeline.sh, so ignoring them would be the usual call — but then
# a clone could not be deployed without a 5-10 minute ffmpeg run first, and the
# point of this repository is that it deploys as-is.
#
# The .mp4 sources are committed too, so the pipeline can be re-run, but they
# are NOT published: .github/workflows/pages.yml assembles the site from the
# derived media only.
